00:32:21.410 --> 00:32:27.970
<v Aviva DeKornfeld>Did you have to ask any questions as part of the investigation that you personally would rather not know?

00:32:27.970 --> 00:33:00.210
<v Vienna Luke>No. Yeah, I wanted to hear everything. Not wanted to, but I think when you spend so many years not knowing, yeah, it feels like just being unsettled for years and years and years, and the unknowns plague you. And I believed that if I had the pieces, that things would make sense to me.

00:33:00.210 --> 00:33:01.390
<v Aviva DeKornfeld>Is that what happened?

00:33:01.390 --> 00:33:43.770
<v Vienna Luke>Yeah, I mean, ultimately, when I say make sense, I mean, that night changed who I was fundamentally, down to my core. It changed me as a person. So actually getting some details on what happened made me realize that I wasn't crazy, that feeling so low, that that was normal based on what had happened.

00:33:43.770 --> 00:33:58.580
<v Aviva DeKornfeld>The one memory Vienna has from the night of Justin taking off her underwear, it had taken years for her to tell anyone about it. It felt too shameful, too private. But now, she brings it up with Justin directly.

00:33:58.580 --> 00:34:05.380
<v Vienna Luke>Did you do anything else to me? Did you go down on me?

00:34:05.380 --> 00:34:09.620
